{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>I will pass through all your flock today; remove from there every speckled and spotted lamb, etc., and it shall be my wages.</b> Those born from now onward that are speckled and spotted among the goats and brown among the sheep shall be mine; and if you find in my flock a different color other than this color, you shall know that it is stolen from me. And Laban answered, 'Behold, would that it be according to your word' — Scripture teaches you that Laban accepted the goats, the majority of which were black; therefore he said, 'every one that is not speckled and spotted among the goats.' And he accepted the ewes, the majority of which were white; therefore he said, 'every brown one among the lambs' — these are the black ones. And because he specified for the he-goats the ring-streaked and the spotted without the speckled, and specified for the goats the speckled and the spotted without the ring-streaked, therefore he needed to say 'every one that is not speckled and spotted among the goats.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:16:33.588719373Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}